1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,000
This is VitalID: prove what matters, and share only what's necessary.

2
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:15,000
Fictional person, synthetic records. A credential prototype with real permissions on Solana devnet, not medical evidence.

3
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:40,000
The recipient has an independent session. As holder, I choose the minimum proof and authorize only this recipient for fifteen minutes. Name and daily measurements are not included.

4
00:00:40,000 --> 00:01:05,000
My browser-held controller signs the permission, and we wait for its real confirmation on Solana devnet.

5
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:25,000
The recipient creates a one-time challenge. The demo issuer signs an assertion about at least seven distinct days of synthetic records.

6
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:45,000
In my browser I derive a BBS selective-disclosure proof, review the presentation, and explicitly authorize sending it.

7
00:01:45,000 --> 00:02:05,000
The recipient verifies the issuer-signed assertion and checks the permission on Solana. BBS verification happens off-chain. The blockchain stores permission state, not health records.

8
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:25,000
Now I revoke future access. Local blocking is immediate; the on-chain revocation is confirmed on devnet.

9
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:40,000
The recipient can no longer request a new presentation. Revocation cannot retrieve information already downloaded.

10
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:55,000
This prototype does not establish clinical truth or authenticate wearable readings. CUDIS and Muse are not connected. VitalID: prove what matters. Share only what's necessary.
